  <div class="post-content"><p>Having a good accountant can be the difference between a business that grows and one that struggles with the IRS every year. Not all accountants are the same — and choosing the wrong one can cost you penalties, tax errors, and money you could have saved. If you own a business in Las Vegas and are looking for an accountant you can trust, this guide is for you.</p><h2>What does a business accountant actually do?</h2><p>A business accountant doesn't just file taxes once a year. A good accountant keeps your books month to month, prepares financial reports, handles your payroll, flags issues before they grow, and represents you if the IRS reaches out. They're basically your business's financial co-pilot.</p><h2>5 Things to Demand From an Accountant in Las Vegas</h2><ol><li>Experience with businesses like yours. An accountant for individuals isn't the same as one who specializes in companies, LLCs, or businesses with employees. Ask directly if they have experience with your type of business.</li><li>Communication in Spanish. If Spanish is your primary language, you need an accountant who explains everything clearly in your language — no confusing translations or terms you don't understand.</li><li>Transparent pricing. A good accountant gives you clear pricing upfront. Be wary of anyone who can't tell you exactly what they charge and why.</li><li>Year-round availability. Accounting work isn't just for tax season. Your accountant should be available when the IRS sends a letter, when you need a report, or whenever you have a question.</li><li>Up-to-date knowledge of tax law. Tax laws change every year. Your accountant should stay current to protect you and make sure you pay only what you owe — no more, no less.</li></ol><h2>What happens if you choose the wrong accountant?</h2><p>An inexperienced accountant can file incorrectly, miss important deductions, or make errors the IRS catches years later. The consequences include penalties, interest, and in serious cases, full audits of your business.</p><h2>Why Las Vegas businesses trust Guzman Tax Accounting</h2><p>At Guzman Tax Accounting, we've spent years working with Latino businesses in Las Vegas. We specialize in business accounting, taxes, payroll, and resolving IRS issues — all in Spanish, with clear pricing and no surprises. Whether you have a new LLC or a business with several employees, we have experience with both. Call us at (725) 340-6758 or reach out on WhatsApp.</p><a href="/en/consultation" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:8px;">Get a Consultation</a></div>
